 "stimulus_html": "<p>Given these pairs of datasets, identify which (if either) would be the best choice for the <i>response</i> variable.</p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 528745,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "A person’s age and their annual income",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "If one variable seems to depend on the other, it is the response (or dependent) variable. The dataset that the response variable depends on is the explanatory (or independent) variable. In this situation, a person’s income depends on age. Age is the response variable."
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Income\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 528746,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "A student’s GPA and their score on the SAT",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "If one variable seems to depend on the other, it is the response (or dependent) variable. The dataset that the response variable depends on is the explanatory (or independent) variable. In this situation, both variables are influenced by a student’s academic ability. So, either could be chosen as the response variable."
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Either; neither one seems to directly influence the other (they’re both influenced by the student’s academic ability)"
    }
   ],
